# What never goes to a host, from any deploy of this repository.
#
# Vercel applies this file to Git deployments as well as CLI uploads, for both
# projects: the website (Root Directory landing) and, since 17 Sep 2026, the
# online clinic app (Root Directory clinicos-app). So clinicos-app itself can no
# longer be excluded whole — the app project would build from an empty folder.
# Instead every place its patient data or secrets can live is excluded by name.
#
# clinicos-app/data/ holds patient records on a clinic computer, and uploading it
# would break invariant 2 in CLAUDE.md — identifiable data never leaves the
# machine. Anything new that holds records, recordings or keys must be added here.
#
# This exists as well as .gitignore, not instead of it: a CLI deploy uploads the
# working tree rather than a git commit, so anything untracked but present on
# disk would otherwise go too.

# Patient data and recordings on a clinic computer, and test copies of them
/clinicos-app/data
/clinicos-app/.local-test
/clinicos-app/.sandbox
/clinicos-app/.test-data
/clinicos-app/logs

# Local transcription: the Python environment and the downloaded model weights
/clinicos-app/asr/.venv
/clinicos-app/asr/models

# Build output and dependencies are rebuilt by the host
/clinicos-app/.next
/clinicos-app/node_modules

# Internal, never part of either site
/portal
/docs
/artifacts
/_to_delete
/Claude outputs
/.claude

*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.zip
.env*
!.env.example
